error[E0277]: a borrowed container of `Rendered` has no storage of its own type: the container's storage holds the runtime's values, not `Rendered`s
  --> tests/compile_fail/borrowed_vec_of_converted.rs:14:1
   |
14 | #[extern_fn(effect = pure)]
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this parameter borrows a container of `Rendered`
   |
help: the trait `InPlaceElement<__R>` is not implemented for `Rendered`
  --> tests/compile_fail/borrowed_vec_of_converted.rs:12:1
   |
12 | pub struct Rendered(());
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: borrow the elements as a slice: the language's `&[Rendered]` and `&mut [Rendered]` are taken as `Slice<Erased<Rt, Rendered>, Shared, Rt>` and `Slice<Erased<Rt, Rendered>, Mut, Rt>`, whose elements read in place as `Rendered` by `as_ref(rt)` and `as_mut(rt)` where `Rendered: Stored<Rt>`; a `Rendered` that is itself `TransparentOver<Rt>`, as an `Erased<Rt, X>` is, is taken as `Slice<Rendered, Shared, Rt>` and `Slice<Rendered, Mut, Rt>` (RFC-0047).
   = note: a `Vec<Rendered>` taken by value materializes each element, and an `async` declaration may take one, which it may not a slice.
help: the trait `InPlaceElement<R>` is implemented for `Erased<R, T>`
  --> $WORKSPACE/acvus-extern/src/erased.rs
   |
   | / impl<R, T> InPlaceElement<R> for Erased<R, T>
   | | where
   | |     R: Runtime,
   | |     T: 'static,
   | |     Self: crate::Branded,
   | |_________________________^
   = note: required for `Vec<Rendered>` to implement `Borrowable<__R>`
   = note: required for `ByRef<Vec<Rendered>, acvus_extern::Shared>` to implement `for<'a, 'w> Arg<'a, 'w, __R>`
   = note: this error originates in the attribute macro `extern_fn` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

